# --- NEVER COMMIT ------------------------------------------------------------
# The identity is a passphrase-encrypted private key. Encrypted is not safe to
# publish: it hands an attacker an offline target they can grind at forever.
# Losing this file loses the DID permanently -- back it up, do not commit it.
identity.pem
identity.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.pkcs8

# Passphrases and anything holding one.
.env
.env.*
*passphrase*
*secret*

# --- fine to commit, and meant to be ------------------------------------------
# receipts/ holds DIDs, signatures and swept text -- all public by construction.
# A receipt is only useful to a third party if they can see it. Not ignored.

# --- local noise ---------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
